1. **A circuit comprising:**

a plurality of externally programmable memory elements configured to store respective data values received from a device external to the circuit;

a first addressing circuit configured to selectively address the externally programmable memory elements for programming or reading the respective data values;

an array comprising a plurality of circuit elements distinct from the externally programmable memory elements; and

a second addressing circuit configured to selectively address the circuit elements of the array independently of the first addressing circuit,

wherein the externally programmable memory elements and the circuit elements of the array are accessible through respective separately addressable address spaces.

1. **An apparatus comprising:**

an array of programmable memory cells arranged in rows and columns;

a plurality of row control lines and a plurality of column control lines coupled to the programmable memory cells;

control circuitry configured to address a selected programmable memory cell by applying respective control signals to at least one of the row control lines and at least one of the column control lines; and

an array of non-memory components, each non-memory component being coupled across a respective control line of a first set of component control lines and a respective control line of a second set of component control lines, the first and second sets of component control lines being distinct from one another.
